  <DT> <H2> <font color="yellow"><font color="red">MAPL</font> = The <font color="red">M</font>aryland <font color="red">A</font>stro<font color="red">P</font>hotonics <font color="red">L</font>aboratory</font> </H2>

<div>
    <p style="float: left; margin: 5px;"><img src="Slide6_cropped.png" height="100px" width="120px">
<br>
<p>
MAPL, the Maryland AstroPhotonics Laboratory, is located in the Jeong
H. Kim Engineering Building on the campus of the University of
Maryland. Co-directed by
Profs. <a HREF="http://www.astro.umd.edu/~veilleux/">Sylvain
Veilleux</a> (ASTR)
and <a HREF="http://www.ece.umd.edu/photonics/">Mario Dagenais</a>
(Electrical and Computer Engineering or ECE), MAPL is used for the
testing, characterization, and integration of astrophotonic components
fabricated in
the <a HREF="https://www.nanocenter.umd.edu/fablab/">FabLab</a> of
the <a HREF="https://www.nanocenter.umd.edu"> Maryland NanoCenter.</a>
</p>
</div>

